00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.400
NICK MARTIN: Good
morning, everybody.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.410
I'm Nick Martin.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.160
I'm head of Google's Cloud
business for retail in the UK.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.130
Well done for making
it here 9:00 AM

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:22.030
on the final day of our
Google NEXT Conference.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.160
We recognize that we had
some stiff competition

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.980
from the party last night and
also, the keynote that's taking

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.470
place at the moment,
so a big well done.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.630
And thank you for
choosing this session

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.330
to spend some time
with us this morning.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.550
I'd like to start the
session with an insight

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.060
into retailers' most
important asset--

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.100
the shopper.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.210
Shoppers today are curious,
demanding, and impatient.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.210
Shoppers have more touch
points with your business

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.990
than ever before.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:53.820
They visit your website.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.130
They use your app.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.440
They come to your
physical store,

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.510
call to your customer
service line,

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:02.960
join your loyalty program,
watch your YouTube videos,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.320
stop by your Facebook page,
subscribe to your email, lists,

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.900
and more.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:12.260
They also see your ads; search,
social, video, TV, radio,

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.660
print, and out of home.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:17.170
So these interactions
produce a wealth

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:19.900
of information
about your customers

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.580
and what they want
from your business.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.540
Good news for business?

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.650
Well, not necessarily,
if that information

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:30.290
is not used effectively.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:33.200
In fact, according to a
joint study Google conducted

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.980
with Greenberg, at
least 62% of people

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:40.730
expect brands to use
their purchase history

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:43.660
to provide them with
personalized experiences.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:47.700
Yet, only 42% think most
brands currently do.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.780
So why is that?

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:52.370
Is it an impossible
task to deliver

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.650
relevant, personalized
experiences at every touch

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:56.980
point?

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.610
What are the reasons
that may prevent this?

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:03.160
Typically, an
organization's data

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:08.380
is spread across many places;
ad campaigns, CRM systems,

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.010
customer service blogs,
website/app analytics, loyalty

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:14.480
programs, and many, many more.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.750
So this means it can be
very, very difficult to get

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.520
a single view of each customer.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.750
So it's no surprise that
almost 60% of marketers,

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.900
according to Forrester,
say that it remains

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.440
difficult to give stakeholders
in different business functions

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.060
access to data and the
insights that they need.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.800
And without it, how can they
create truly personalized

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.100
experiences?

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.140
But to deliver that
kind of experience

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.530
that your customer now
expects, organizations

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:50.630
need to take a very
different approach.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:53.400
The key thing is you need
to have all of your data--

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.980
not just some of your data--

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:58.460
in one place, structured
and unstructured,

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.560
all different types.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.130
And when it's in one place, then
you're in a position to unlock

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:08.230
the most valuable
insights it provides.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.830
Cloud Solutions enable you
to break down data silos

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.830
and organize your data
such that you can better

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:18.790
analyze and activate it
to gain better insights

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.985
and drive better and
more predictive outcomes.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:28.450
We speak with many
organizations who are actively

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.540
working to incorporate
artificial intelligence

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:36.590
and machine learning into
their data analytics strategy.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.920
Yet, the vast majority
of those organizations

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:43.490
are at the very earliest
stage of AI initiative.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:47.300
According to the Gartner
survey, the CIO survey

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:52.160
last year, it's reckoned
that only 4% of CIOs

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:56.420
currently have AI under way
within the organization.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.016
Yet, this is set
to change rapidly

00:03:59.016 --> 00:04:00.390
over the next two
to three years.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:05.390
In fact, it's reckoned by 2020,
more than 85% of organizations

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:08.300
will have AI
programs under pilot

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.530
or in an operational mode.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.940
So why is that?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:19.709
Well, to adopt AI, customers
face many, many challenges.

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:25.100
Technology-- the scale needed
to handle AI is massive.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:26.960
From an operational
perspective, you

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:30.990
need to have the right expertise
in place, the right people.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:34.110
But very few organizations
have those people--

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.960
they're a scarce breed--

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.110
and tooling, which, to date,
has been very narrow in terms

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:43.780
of the options that it
provides and requiring

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:47.080
much specialization.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:50.020
So realistically,
AI has only been

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.810
in the hands of very few
people, very few organizations

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.970
in the last few decades.

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:58.510
And it's those who've had
access to deep computational

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:02.170
resources, training, and
specialized expertise

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.990
in machine learning,
organizations

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:09.330
that are technology-oriented.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.980
So you need to
embrace new approaches

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:14.430
and adopt technologies like
artificial intelligence,

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.940
but doing that is a huge
operational challenge.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.530
This is where Google
Cloud comes in.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:23.860
Google Cloud is Google's
public cloud computing business

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.440
and brings a variety of
products and services

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.860
to provide you with AI at scale.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.870
So why choose Google for AI?

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:38.450
Well, we provide that massive
scale, the same computing power

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:42.650
that powers Google
Search, Gmail, Maps,

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:46.970
Android, and many others which
have over a billion users

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:48.910
today.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:52.240
We provide high performance,
a global infrastructure

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.400
as a service, leveraging
Google's technology

00:05:54.400 --> 00:06:00.140
and servers, processes,
and private fiber network,

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:03.810
and quality of technology with
a range of innovations Google

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:07.290
has developed for data
management, analytics,

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:11.420
and artificial intelligence.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:15.110
And bringing together
customization for a Cloud AI

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:20.180
solution with an approach we
take to do advance solution

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:21.830
labs where we will
develop innovation

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.990
with you, our
professional services

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:27.560
capability, and the extensive
range of business partners

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:30.380
that Google has is how
we bring this to you

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:33.890
to provide that AI capability
in your organization

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.628
and improve your productivity.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:42.070
We provide a spectrum of
AI machine learning tools.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.860
And you would have heard some
of these being further announced

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:47.130
during this conference.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:50.590
And this is enabling you to
leverage your organization's

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:55.240
capabilities and skill sets, and
also your big asset in client.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:07:00.070
On one end, we have pre-trained
out-of-the-box models

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:03.940
for companies that don't really
have that expertise in-house.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.620
And you can use
pre-trained models

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:11.320
like Vision API, Video API,
Video Analysis, Natural

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:15.520
Language API, or Translation API
to deliver certain experiences

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:18.630
to your customer.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.190
On the other end
of the scale, you

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:23.160
have Google's market
leading open source machine

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.770
learning engine
TensorFlow, which

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:29.280
lets your data scientists
build their own models to solve

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:33.020
customer challenges
within your business.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:35.240
And in the middle, we
offer manage services

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:38.270
like Cloud ML that brings
the best of both worlds

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:42.770
together so you can customize
models for specific use,

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.110
but use our manage
services to test,

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.210
train, and scale your
models in the Cloud.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.780
Now, enough for me.

