00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:01.390
So to answer your
question, what is Ocado?

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:04.540
And what businesses
are in Ocado?

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:08.930
So quickly, by a show of
hands, who has heard of Ocado

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:11.490
or interacted with Ocado?

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.270
OK, Good.

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:14.700
So that means my colleagues
who have been speaking also

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.920
at some other sessions
have done a good job,

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.230
because there's some hands up.

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:23.140
Who's used Ocado before?

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:25.200
So very few hands.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:28.860
So basically, Ocado,
at a high level,

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:32.670
is really a fusion
of two businesses.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:35.950
On the one side, we
have a retail business,

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:37.620
which, if you've
lived in the UK,

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:41.100
or you've actually used the
service, or been into London

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.200
and seen some of
the vans, you'll

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:46.710
know that we run an online
grocery supermarket where

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:48.450
we take orders in.

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:51.630
And through a series of
supply chain activities,

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.977
we then deliver an order
to people's houses.

00:09:53.977 --> 00:09:55.560
And actually, we go
further than that.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.800
We go into the kitchen and
deliver it into the kitchen.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.849
So it's a great
end-to-end service

00:10:00.849 --> 00:10:02.640
where you can have your
groceries delivered

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:04.650
in a one hour time slot.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:08.130
That's our retail
side of the business.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:12.540
And depending that we have
a technology business, which

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:15.120
actually is only really
come to light over

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:18.270
the last few years
in the public eye,

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:24.270
the technology business focuses
on building the platform

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:27.250
that powers that
retail business.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:30.120
So things that are
important are all

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.750
of the learnings
that are happening

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:35.820
in the retail business, all
of the specific customer

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:41.220
requirements, and then this
real-time feedback loop

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:44.630
that we get from our retail
customers interacting

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:46.680
with the Ocado brand.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:50.280
So what you have here
is this unique fusion

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:53.730
of two businesses with
an amazing feedback

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:55.314
loop that's real-time.

00:10:55.314 --> 00:10:56.730
So on the one side,
we're learning

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:59.550
from customers, because we
have an online supermarket.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:02.490
And on the other side,
we're building technology

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:04.010
to support that service.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:08.970
So then, who is Ocado?

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:14.190
So Ocado is the world's largest
dedicated online grocery

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.700
retailer.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:19.230
We have over 600,000
active shoppers.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:22.950
We have a range of
over 50,000 SKUs

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:26.070
across our four
automated warehouses.

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:32.980
And we pick around a quarter
of a million orders per week.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:37.350
So for an online-only
business with no stores,

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:38.856
that's quite big.

00:11:38.856 --> 00:11:40.230
Just to give you
an understanding

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:43.260
of the number of orders,
this is a picture

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:48.030
which was taken actually in
San Francisco on an ad for Sony

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:49.920
BRAVIA.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:53.760
They released a whole lot of
bouncing balls into the street.

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:57.360
And actually, they
released 250,000 balls,

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:00.900
so just to give you perspective
on the kind of number

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:05.100
of orders we're doing in a
week through our automated

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:05.880
facilities.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:13.680
So then, taking the
lens and looking

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:17.370
through that second business,
which is our technology

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:22.960
business, the question is, what
is the Ocado Smart Platform?

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:26.730
So this is our modular and
scalable software and hardware

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:30.300
platform, designed to put
the world's largest retailers

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:31.690
online.

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:34.380
So we currently
have some partners,

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:36.480
which you would have
seen in the press

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:39.930
releases over the
last year or so,

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:42.420
who have engaged
in this platform.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:45.870
And what the platform
aids to do is

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:49.050
to deliver a full
end-to-end service

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:51.720
for your retail business.

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:55.650
So there are three key
activities over here

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:59.470
which we focus on within
our end-to-end platform.

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:03.400
The first activity
is that of shopping.

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:07.320
So we create an
interface where customers

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:11.010
can come to a website,
and engage with the site,

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:14.340
and shop, and add favorites,
et cetera, et cetera,

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:16.290
and build a basket.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:20.860
Once that's complete, we then
have to fulfill that order.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:22.320
So we have to pick it.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:25.680
And we have our
automated facilities.

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:28.860
And we also have an
in-store picking system.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:32.150
And then once that order
is picked and fulfilled,

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:34.450
we then need to deliver
it to the customer.

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:37.080
So the third part is delivery.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:39.720
And that's where we
load up our vans.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:42.960
And using proprietary routing
systems and algorithms,

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:49.170
we deliver the groceries to our
users, either in their homes

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:52.390
or via click and
collect-type portals.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:02.910
So an image, which, from
a product perspective,

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:07.290
is a lot easier to get your head
around what the platform is,

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:11.760
would be to try dividing
into these triangles, where,

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:13.380
as I mentioned, you
have the shopping

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:17.070
experience in the top half
of the triangles, which

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:21.570
is responsible for the
ecommerce activities.

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:25.860
You then have our fulfillment
triangle, effectively,

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:29.920
or module, which is responsible
for fulfilling those orders.

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:32.260
And then you have
our delivery module,

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:35.780
which is responsible for
sending them to clients.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:40.170
And they are all held
